# uart: a transmitter and a receiver behind one baud divisor. The package
# ships eight modules in **four files and two layers**, and the file count
# is not an accident: a design that reaches this library through
# `reticle fpga` names its sources by hand, and three test suites and four
# example READMEs in this repository name exactly these four paths. So each
# configurable module lives in the same file as the fixed-format facade
# built on it, and adding the character format added no file for anybody to
# have to list. README.md §2 says it at length.
#
#   rtl/uart_tx.v        uart_frame_tx, then uart_tx
#   rtl/uart_rx.v        uart_frame_rx, then uart_rx
#   rtl/uart.v           uart_frame, then uart
#   rtl/uart_baud_div.v  uart_baud_div, then uart_line_coding
#
# `top` names `uart`, which is the 8N1-by-default pair a design with a
# fixed framing wants, and a design that wants only one half instantiates
# `uart_tx` or `uart_rx` directly. The `uart_frame*` modules are the same
# hardware with the character format on **ports** instead of parameters,
# which is what a USB serial port needs: `uart_baud_div` turns a bit rate
# into the `div` every one of them takes, and `uart_line_coding` turns a
# host's SET_LINE_CODING into the format the frame modules take — so that
# a host's `stty` reaches the wire and not just a register.
name uart
version 1.1.0
license MIT
description "UART transmitter and receiver with a ready/valid interface, selectable data bits, parity and stop bits, distinguished receive errors, and a run-time or parameterised baud divisor"

top uart
target ice40
target ecp5

source rtl/uart_tx.v
source rtl/uart_rx.v
source rtl/uart.v
source rtl/uart_baud_div.v

param CLK_DIV int 16 4..65535
param DATA_BITS int 8 5..8
param PARITY int 0 0..4
param STOP_BITS int 1 1..2

port clk in
port rst_n in
port div in 16
port tx_data in 8
port tx_valid in
port tx_ready out
port tx out
port rx in
port rx_data out 8
port rx_valid out
port rx_error out
port rx_frame_error out
port rx_parity_error out
port rx_break out
